class MeetingHostRpcSendAnswer(BaseModel):
    """
    The 200 answer to send. sent: the invitation exists at Google and receipt says what was made; tilo-api checks it (HB-07) before storing it. refused: nothing was sent and nothing will be (SideEffectRefused, HB-03 to HB-06). possibly_sent: Google may hold the invitation and a retry would not help (PossiblySent). retry: try again later; may_have_sent is false when nothing reached Google (not connected, expired, a missing scope, a KMS outage) and true after a Google 5xx or a lost answer. receipt is set only with sent and may_have_sent only with retry; otherwise each is null. parts lists what the broker emitted during the call; tilo-connectors writes no data.transfer and raises no alert of its own outbox here, because tilo-api's outbox does (one writer per world).
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    outcome: Literal["sent", "refused", "possibly_sent", "retry"]
    receipt: MeetingHostRpcReceipt | None
    may_have_sent: bool | None
    parts: MeetingHostRpcParts


class MeetingHostRpcDisconnectAnswer(BaseModel):
    """
    The 200 answer to disconnect. revoked_at_provider is true only when Google confirmed the revoke. The call is idempotent: with nothing stored it answers false with no parts. parts carries connection.revoked, and an alert.raised for each revoke kept for a retry.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    revoked_at_provider: bool
    parts: MeetingHostRpcParts


class MeetingHostRpcViewsAnswer(BaseModel):
    """
    The 200 answer to POST /internal/connections/views (ADR-0032 addendum 1, HB-08, HB-09): the connection views of the request's user_id, one per stored grant of a connector that config/connectors.yaml declares with auth oauth2, in registry order, each connector at most once. A connector with no stored grant is absent (tilo-api shows it available); a disconnect deletes the grant, so it is absent too. A store read only, with no token use, no KMS call, no provider call and no event, so it has no parts. At most 32 views. tilo-api treats an answer that breaks this contract or HB-09 as unknown as a whole, never as partly read.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    views: Annotated[list[MeetingHostRpcConnectionView], Field(max_length=32)]


class Meter(BaseModel):
    """
    The HUD meter's state for one run (PRD 14.4, FR-MTR-07): credits used (the sum of the run's event credits), credits saved (origin cost minus lookup cost over accepted reuses, PRD 14.3), time saved (estimate) and the run's budget. packages/metering computes it from the run's events up to last_seq, and apps/web renders it. Rules MT-05 and MT-06 in contracts/metering.rules.md.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    run_id: RunId
    last_seq: Annotated[int, Field(ge=0)]
    """
    seq of the last event this state includes. A client shows a state only if its last_seq is higher than the one on screen (MT-06).
    """
    credits_used: Credits
    credits_saved: Credits
    time_saved: MeterTimeSaved
    budget: MeterBudget


class Metering(BaseModel):
    """
    config/metering.yaml: the Treasury's settings (PRD 14.1, 14.4, 17.3; FR-MTR-02, -03, -04, -08). What the PRD states as a rule is const: the 15% reserve, the budget request at 80% and the reconciliation tolerance of 10%. Caps and daily spend limits are config with the PRD demo defaults. The credit unit (US$0.005) stays in config/prices.yaml. Rules a schema cannot express are MT-01.. in contracts/metering.rules.md.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    treasury: MeteringTreasury
    caps: MeteringCaps
    spend: MeteringSpend
    reconciliation: MeteringReconciliation


class Person(BaseModel):
    """
    A person of an org (PRD 15.1 User entity, ADR-0015): who they are, how they are called in a meeting, how Tilo reaches them, and which teams an org owner put them in. `aliases` are names others use for them; a spoken name that matches more than one person is never assigned (PE-15). A membership counts only as people.rules.md defines it (PE-02). Contact details are never shown to teammates; `tilo-api` resolves a recipient from this record (PE-09).
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    id: UserId
    org_id: OrgId
    display_name: Annotated[
        str, Field(max_length=80, min_length=1, pattern="^[^\\u0000-\\u001F\\u007F]+$")
    ]
    aliases: Annotated[list[Alias], Field(max_length=8)]
    email: EmailAddress
    time_zone: Annotated[
        str,
        Field(
            max_length=64, pattern="^(UTC|[A-Z][A-Za-z_+-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+){1,2})$"
        ),
    ]
    """
    IANA time zone name (Asia/Kolkata) or UTC: the zone of due dates and the reminder window.
    """
    preferred_channel: Literal["web", "mobile_web", "email"]
    """
    Where Tilo reaches the person: in the app (web, mobile_web) or by email (FR-PB-03). Narrower than the common channel list on purpose: no new record names a channel outside these three.
    """
    org_role: Literal["owner", "member"]
    memberships: Annotated[list[PersonMembership], Field(max_length=8)]
    created_by: TeamLeadAssignment


class Plan(BaseModel):
    """
    PlanGraph (PRD 7.1 FR-INT-06, FR-INT-09): the approaches offered, the chosen one compiled to units, dependencies, roles, skills, connectors and gates, and the confirmed budget cap. Cross-reference rules PG-01.. are in contracts/plan.rules.md.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    approaches: Annotated[list[PlanApproach], Field(max_length=3, min_length=2)]
    chosen_approach: PlanApproachId
    """
    id of the approach the user picked (PG-07).
    """
    units: Annotated[list[PlanUnit], Field(max_length=200, min_length=1)]
    gates: Annotated[list[PlanGate], Field(max_length=100)]
    budget_cap: Annotated[float, Field(gt=0.0)]
    """
    Budget cap in credits the user confirmed (FR-INT-08).
    """


class Plate(BaseModel):
    """
    A person's plate (FR-PA-02, ADR-0021): a read model tilo-api builds per request for the signed-in person only, never stored and never an event (PE-26). S-27, the digest and the panel read the same `rows`; `parked` holds the person's own snoozed, reassign-asked and recently done work items for S-27 only (PE-27). Groups and order are code (PE-28): `today` is the date in the person's time zone at `as_of`. A row is a reference with at most a title (PE-29). `truncated` says more rows passing PE-26 and PE-27 exist than a full lane holds (200 rows or 100 parked), so it is true only with a full lane (PE-27); `fingerprint` is the SHA-256 of `rows` as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace (PE-30).
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    v: Literal["1.0"]
    user: UserId
    as_of: Timestamp
    today: CalendarDate
    rows: Annotated[list[PlatePlateRow], Field(max_length=200)]
    parked: Annotated[list[PlatePlateRow], Field(max_length=100)]
    truncated: bool
    fingerprint: Annotated[str, Field(max_length=64, pattern="^[0-9a-f]{64}$")]


class PolicyRiskTierTable(BaseModel):
    """
    Risk tiers (PRD 10.4): each action type's base tier, the context modifiers that raise any action to T3, and the highest level each tier allows. A modifier applies whatever the base tier, so a deletion or an external share is T3 even when its action type is listed lower.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    actions: Annotated[dict[ActionType, RiskTier], Field(min_length=1)]
    modifiers: Annotated[list[PolicyTierModifier], Field(max_length=6, min_length=6)]
    """
    All six PRD 10.4 T3 conditions, each exactly once: six unique items over a closed six-value enum with a fixed raises_to, so none can be dropped.
    """
    max_level: PolicyMaxLevel


class Providers(BaseModel):
    """
    Provider-layer configuration as the provider layer loads it (PRD 6.4, 6.6, 14.1): models is config/models.yaml ($defs.models) and prices is config/prices.yaml ($defs.prices). The loader also checks that every role names existing profiles and every profile has a price entry, and the speech role's rules below (1.2.0, ADR-0027). Model ids appear only in config/ and packages/providers.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    models: ProvidersModels
    prices: ProvidersPrices


type UiAction = Annotated[
    UiActionNavigate | UiActionMarkDone | UiActionSnooze | UiActionDraftReply | UiActionTag | UiActionUntag,
    Field(title="UiAction"),
]
"""
The allow-list of what the assistant panel may do on the page (FR-PA-14, PE-10): a closed union on `kind`. The web app has one executor that maps each kind to a handler; a document that does not validate is dropped, so a model can never click, type, read the page or go anywhere outside these routes and targets. State-changing kinds act on the signed-in person's own records through the same API routes as the buttons; `draft_reply` makes a draft (T1) and sends nothing; no kind sends to another person.
"""


class ArtifactVersionManifestRevision(BaseModel):
    """
    One append-only revision of a version's provenance manifest, at .../versions/{version:06d}/manifests/{n:04d} (AR-06): created at put, reviewed after the Verifier (cause its artifact.reviewed), sent (cause the data.transfer out) or exported when the version leaves Tilo. Readers take the highest n.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    n: Annotated[int, Field(ge=1, le=9999)]
    stage: Literal["created", "reviewed", "sent", "exported"]
    cause: Ulid | None
    manifest: Manifest


class Brief(BaseModel):
    """
    Structured brief the Director extracts from intake (PRD 7.1 FR-INT-03, FR-INT-04, FR-INT-05). Every field is an editable chip; empty arrays are allowed, missing keys are not.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    goal: Annotated[str, Field(max_length=500, min_length=1)]
    deliverables: Annotated[list[BriefDeliverable], Field(max_length=10, min_length=1)]
    audience: Annotated[str, Field(max_length=200, min_length=1)]
    deadline: CalendarDate | None
    """
    Due date, or null when the task has none.
    """
    constraints: Annotated[list[Constraint], Field(max_length=20)]
    sources: Annotated[list[BriefSource], Field(max_length=50)]
    sensitivity: DataClass
    """
    Most sensitive class of data the task touches (PRD 12.1 data classes; ADR-0002).
    """
    assumptions: Annotated[list[BriefAssumption], Field(max_length=10)]
    """
    FR-INT-04: what was assumed instead of asking, shown as "Assumed: ...".
    """
    applied_preferences: Annotated[list[BriefAppliedPreference], Field(max_length=20)]
    """
    FR-INT-05: preferences and past answers applied from memory instead of asking, each with its citation.
    """


class CardGate(BaseModel):
    """
    The exact action a gate card holds. The deterministic card builder copies it from the plan gate, the connector action and the proposed side effect (the outbox entry the gate releases); the card validator rejects any mismatch (card.rules.md CR-09 to CR-12).
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    id: GateId
    action: CardGateAction
    recipients: Annotated[list[EmailAddress], Field(max_length=50)]
    irreversible: bool
    risk_tier: RiskTier


class AssistantRepliedData(BaseModel):
    """
    data of assistant.replied (CC-PEOPLE, FR-PA-13, -14, -19, PE-10, PE-11). The panel answered. decided_by says whether deterministic rules or the cheap model picked the read model or action; the answer text is a template over read-model rows and sits in the raw archive (message_ref). sources are the records every claim cites (HR-1): an answered outcome has at least one. ui_action is the one validated allow-list action the panel took or offers; a navigated outcome has one. cached is true when the answer was served from an unchanged-records cache.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    conversation_id: Ulid
    message_ref: EventArchiveRef
    outcome: Literal["answered", "navigated", "declined", "failed"]
    decided_by: Literal["rules", "model"]
    sources: Annotated[list[RecordRef], Field(max_length=20)]
    ui_action: UiAction | None
    cached: bool


class LayoutLevel(BaseModel):
    """
    A phase of the work; levels stack as plates.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    id: LevelId
    name: PlainName
    districts: Annotated[list[LayoutDistrict], Field(max_length=6, min_length=1)]


class MeetingHostRpcSendRequest(BaseModel):
    """
    POST /internal/meeting-host/send, called only by the host run's outbox stub in tilo-api (HB-02). entry is the outbox entry (outbox.schema.json) tilo-api's outbox enqueued, evidence the case its enqueue checked, and draft the pinned item the owner approved. It names no user: the grant used is (entry.authz.ref, meeting_host). The then branch narrows entry to the one action this surface runs (MH-10), a meeting invitation the owner approved: state queued, create_meeting_event on meeting_host, T3 with the new_recipients modifier, 1 to 50 recipients (MAX_RECIPIENTS), no attachments, the draft pinned as item, the host account's primary calendar as destination, no undo window, authorised by a person. (The narrowing sits in if/then so the generated type stays Outbox.)
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    entry: Outbox
    evidence: MeetingHostRpcEvidence
    draft: MeetingHostRpcDraft


class Card(BaseModel):
    """
    One card, every channel (PRD 10.2, 10.3): needs-you, gate, consent and meeting cards. Channel rules are data: answer_channels is limited per kind (email answers questions only; gates need sign-in on the web or a verified WhatsApp number; consent needs the web). safe_default is the option id applied at timeout; it names one of the options and that option is reversible (contracts/card.rules.md CR-01 to CR-03). A gate's or consent card's is always hold, so a gate never times out to go and a consent card never times out to a grant; every hold option is reversible, only a gate may offer an irreversible option, and neither a gate nor a consent card is delegated to the Director. A gate's option ids are the closed set approve, edit, hold, each with a fixed label (Approve, Edit first, Hold); only approve opens the gate, and its irreversible flag equals the gate's (CR-07, CR-08). A consent card's option ids are the closed set connect, hold with fixed labels Connect, Hold; only connect grants (CR-13). The deterministic card builder writes a gate card's gate details and options, never a model, and the card validator checks them against the plan gate, the connector action and the outbox entry the gate releases (CR-09 to CR-12).
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    id: Ulid
    world_id: WorldId
    run_id: RunId
    kind: CardKind
    rung: Literal["needs_you", "blocked", "meeting", "gate", "consent"]
    """
    Escalation ladder rung (PRD 10.2); needs_you cards may be blocked.
    """
    header: CardHeader
    what_happened: Annotated[str, Field(max_length=140, min_length=1)]
    why_it_matters: Annotated[str, Field(max_length=280, min_length=1)]
    options: CardOptions
    add_context: bool
    """
    Whether the card offers the add-context field.
    """
    actions: list[Literal["show_me", "snooze", "delegate"]]
    answer_channels: Annotated[list[Channel], Field(min_length=1)]
    created_at: Timestamp
    timeout: Annotated[int, Field(ge=1)]
    """
    Seconds after created_at when the safe default applies and the Director posts a Nudge.
    """
    safe_default: CardOptionId
    gate: CardGate | None
    """
    Set on gate cards only.
    """
    consent: CardConsent | None
    """
    Set on consent cards only.
    """


class LayoutSemantic(BaseModel):
    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    levels: Annotated[list[LayoutLevel], Field(min_length=1)]
    islands: list[LayoutIsland]
    gates: list[LayoutGate]
    agents: Annotated[list[LayoutAgent], Field(min_length=1)]


type MeetingHostRpc = Annotated[
    MeetingHostRpcSendRequest | MeetingHostRpcSendAnswer | MeetingHostRpcUserRequest | MeetingHostRpcStatusAnswer | MeetingHostRpcDisconnectAnswer | MeetingHostRpcViewsAnswer | MeetingHostRpcError,
    Field(title="MeetingHostRpc"),
]
"""
The internal surface of tilo-connectors that tilo-api calls (FR-MTG-09, ADR-0032 decision 2 and addendum 1): what tilo-api posts to /internal/meeting-host/send, /internal/meeting-host/status, /internal/meeting-host/disconnect and /internal/connections/views, and what each answers. Each route validates its own request and answer ($defs send_request and send_answer; user_request and status_answer; user_request and disconnect_answer; user_request and views_answer; error for any refusal) in both services; this root is any one of them. Every object is closed, and no field holds an access or refresh token, an OAuth code, the client secret, key material or a Meet link (ADR-0024 decision 4, ADR-0032 decision 3). Ids travel in the body, never in a path or query. A route refuses a body over 65536 bytes (64 KiB) before it parses it. Rules that compare values (HB-03 the draft against its hash and the entry, HB-05 the owner, HB-07 the receipt against the entry, HB-09 the views against config/connectors.yaml) are checked by the routes and by tilo-api's client, not by this schema. 1.1.0 adds views_answer, connection_view and scope (additive).
"""


class Layout(BaseModel):
    """
    WorldLayout v1 (PRD 9.2). A model writes semantic; only the deterministic solver writes geometry (null until solved). Rules WE-01.. that a schema cannot express are in contracts/layout.rules.md.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra="forbid",
    )
    v: Literal["1.0"]
    world_id: WorldId
    tier: Tier
    theme: Slug
    """
    World theme from config/themes/.
    """
    semantic: LayoutSemantic
    geometry: LayoutGeometry | None


